-> `∪`/`∩` materialize an unresolved-but-FINITE domain into a Set (see
-> set_op_domain_materialize.code). An unbounded domain still can't be
-> enumerated — must be rejected, not hang trying, same as
-> fail_loop_unbounded_domain.code for the `loop <var> { }` form that
-> shares this same underlying finite_candidates() engine.
a = {5}
b ∈ Z
b > 3
c = a ∪ b
